    "body": "1. Yes, a memory command triggers a PIM operation, and the PIM operation, including `readOpd()` which fetches operands from bank or register, is executed within DRAM timing constraints.\r\n\r\n2. The data can be fetched directly from an active row into a register in the PIM Block. The bank address where the data is located comes from the memory controller, and the register address is controlled by the PIM block. As mentioned above, the entire process performed in one memory command.",
